<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia says CPI rises 0.27 percent in August.</title>
<headline>Indonesia says CPI rises 0.27 percent in August.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's consumer price index (CPI) rose 0.27 percent month-on-month in August compared to 0.68 percent in July, Information Minister Harmoko said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said food prices fell 0.35 percent but housing costs rose 0.27 percent, textiles were up 0.16 percent and services rose 1.16 percent.</p>
<p>CPI (pct)	     August 96     July 96     August 95</p>
<p>Month/month	    +0.27	   +0.68	  +0.32</p>
<p>Year/year		+7.21	   +7.26	  +8.80</p>
</text>
